preConditionHook:
// GRIMES'S NAMED ANTI TEMPLATE (G06-40, G16-01), the PRICE-STRUCTURE form he
// prefers -- merge decision 6 leaves Linda Raschke's stochastic original to
// AntiStochasticSlopeDisagreement. A trend shows a pattern suggesting it could
// be ending, a countertrend swing afterwards emerges that is much stronger than the
// trend's previous countertrend swings, and the trade is the FIRST PULLBACK
// after that swing, entered in the direction of the NEW move. A trend
// TERMINATION trade, so the SHORT is the one taken after an UPTREND shows its
// cracks.
//
// THREE PARTS IN SEQUENCE -- setup, change of character, trigger:
//   1. TREND TERMINATION PRECONDITION (TrendTerminationPrecondition, G06-33).
//      A merge working name that appears in no slice: the merged
//      climax_termination bucket DROPPED it as "composition (an OR) of
//      MomentumDivergenceAtSwingExtreme, LargeRangeBarInWindow and FailureTest
//      -- the Anti's first setup condition, carried by the named Anti template
//      rather than as a rule", which is what is inlined here. Its "double top
//      or bottom" sub-case is the DoubleExtreme* family and is left to its own
//      pane, as that drop note says.
//   2. A COUNTERTREND SWING STRONGER THAN THE PRIOR ONES
//      (CountertrendSpikeStrongerThanPriorSwings, G06-34, also a working name
//      in no slice): the on-disk SwingLegExceedsAverageLeg, whose row records
//      G06-34 as one of its two sources -- its SHORT side measures the newest
//      DOWN leg against the mean of the prior down legs, which is exactly
//      "in an uptrend, a downswing much stronger than previous downswings".
//   3. THE FIRST PULLBACK AFTER THAT SWING (AntiFirstPullbackTrigger, G06-35):
//      the on-disk FirstPullbackAfterSpike, which the merged catalog_match
//      already names as the Anti's trigger alone.
//
// WHY IT IS ONE FILE, on three counts: part 1 is an OR of three, so no pane-AND
// reaches it; the parts are ORDERED IN TIME rather than simultaneous; and the
// ordering needs CROSS-BAR STATE that only a rule can keep.
//
// THE ORDERING IS A LATCH, not a re-evaluation of part 1 at every past bar.
// Part 1 is evaluated on THIS bar and its age is carried in state -- a `seen`
// bool plus a bar counter, the FailedFinalFlagTrendResumption construction --
// and the trade needs the precondition to have fired within recentLookback
// bars. The counter is incremented BEFORE the latch, so an event on this bar
// gives age 0 and the trade may fire on the same bar; the `seen` bool is what
// keeps a never-fired precondition from reading as age 0 during warm-up, since
// an EL variable holds 0 before its first assignment. Parts 2 and 3 are read on
// this bar: the leg test rests on confirmed pivots and so persists for several
// bars after the leg completes, and the trigger carries its own maxWaitBars
// window.
//
// SIDES ARE MIXED ACROSS THE PARTS, which is the other thing panes could not
// assemble. The Anti's SHORT needs: the divergence read that
// MomentumDivergenceAtSwingExtreme puts on its LONG side (a new price extreme the
// oscillator does not confirm -- Grimes's bearish divergence, as that rule's
// own row records), the failure test that FailedBreakoutReversal puts on its
// SHORT side (a poke above resistance, closing back under), the leg test on
// SwingLegExceedsAverageLeg's SHORT side, and FirstPullbackAfterSpike's SHORT
// side. No placement can borrow another side's condition.
//
// THE OSCILLATOR IS MERGE DECISION 2's 3/10: the fastLen-bar simple average of
// the closing price minus the slowLen-bar one, both simple averages recomputed from price every bar (EL
// Average is not rolling), never the MACD word. osc is an EL VARIABLE, so its
// [ii] history is the variable's own and is mirrored in the C++ twin by a
// zero-seeded ring buffer, re-seeded when the depth changes; divReady guards
// the warm-up on CurrentBar. DIVERGENCE IS DECISION 3: WINDOW MAXIMA, no pivot
// scan.
//
// THE FAILURE TEST IS FailedBreakoutReversal AND BodyExceedsAverageBarRange,
// which is what the FailureTest key reduces to -- an excursion beyond the
// shifted window extreme within failBars bars, reclaimed by this bar's close,
// with a body bigger than bodyMultiple times the mean BAR RANGE (the mean
// range, not the mean body: that is BodyExceedsAverageBarRange's harder test
// and the one Grimes's rejection bar needs). The per-candidate level is
// open-coded because it is a history reference on a function call at a VARIABLE
// offset; Extremes() is EL source and is exactly the loop.
//
// ONE lookback SERVES FOUR WINDOWS -- the divergence maxima, the climax bar's
// range benchmark, the failure test's level window and its body benchmark --
// which is what keeps the input count at 14 rather than 17. The pivot scan
// keeps its own pivotLookback because it counts pivots, not bars.
//
// MEASURED SWING PIVOT (decision 14): the three-occurrence scan is hand-rolled
// verbatim from SwingLegExceedsAverageLeg, because SwingHigh Occurrence 3+ is
// UNMEASURED. numLegs is the number of PRIOR legs averaged, so numLegs + 1
// pivots are needed per series and the scan caps it at 2; G06-34's own three
// prior swings are OUT OF REACH and recorded rather than approximated.
// legMultiple defaults to G06-34's 1.5. Existence is guarded by the pivot
// COUNTS, never by a price compared with -1.
//
// For GUARDS at >= 1 (or >= 2 where a window is scanned from its second bar):
// EasyLanguage's For counts DOWN when the end value is below the start, so an
// empty window would read bars the C++ for-loops never touch.
//
// SHIFT TEST: the oscillator is a difference of two means of the same series,
// the divergence compares it with its own window peak, and every price term is
// a difference or a window extreme of the same series.
//
// THE LOOSE VARIANT IS DROPPED: G06-36's "enter anywhere into that first
// pullback" has no bar test of its own, per the merge note.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(lookback + slowLen - 1, failBars + lookback,
// pivotLookback - 1 + strength, maxWaitBars + spikeBars + 1).
//
// THE C++ TWIN WRITES OUT BY HAND what the EL twin says with built-ins. The
// window extremes mirror Extremes(), EL SOURCE -- seeded on the window's first
// bar, continued with a STRICT comparison under the EL relational tolerance.
// The oscillator's own history is the zero-seeded RING BUFFER, depth
// lookback + 1, re-seeded when the depth changes, exactly as
// MomentumDivergenceAtSwingExtreme and AtrRising do; reading close[i] again
// instead would use bars EasyLanguage never saw. The three-occurrence pivot
// scan is written WITHOUT break and with the < 3 counters, statement for
// statement with the EL twin.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement; loop counters and
// per-candidate flags are block-scoped inside their loops. THE FOUR LATCH
// LOCALS (seenUp/seenDn, ageUp/ageDn) are DELIBERATELY not reset at the top of
// the hook -- they are the state -- and a second placement gets its own copy.
oscFast = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)fastLen; ++i) {
    oscFast += close[i];
}
oscFast = oscFast / (int)fastLen;
oscSlow = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)slowLen; ++i) {
    oscSlow += close[i];
}
oscSlow = oscSlow / (int)slowLen;
osc = oscFast - oscSlow;
oscDepth = (int)lookback + 1;
if (oscDepth < 2) {
    oscDepth = 2;
}
if (oscHistory.size() != (std::size_t)oscDepth) {
    oscHistory.assign((std::size_t)oscDepth, 0.0);
    oscCursor = 0;
}
oscHistory[oscCursor] = osc;
oscCursor = (oscCursor + 1) % oscHistory.size();
pHigh = high[1];
pLow = low[1];
oscPeak = oscHistory[(oscCursor + oscHistory.size() - 2) % oscHistory.size()];
oscTrough = oscPeak;
for (int ii = 2; ii <= (int)lookback; ++ii) {
    if (el_gt(high[ii], pHigh)) pHigh = high[ii];
    if (el_lt(low[ii], pLow)) pLow = low[ii];
    double v = oscHistory[(oscCursor + oscHistory.size() - 1 - (std::size_t)ii) % oscHistory.size()];
    if (el_gt(v, oscPeak)) oscPeak = v;
    if (el_lt(v, oscTrough)) oscTrough = v;
}
divReady = ctx.CurrentBar() > (int)lookback;
divUp = divReady && el_ge(high[0], pHigh) && el_lt(osc, oscPeak);
divDn = divReady && el_le(low[0], pLow) && el_gt(osc, oscTrough);
rangeSum = 0.0;
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int jj = 1; jj <= (int)lookback; ++jj) {
    rangeSum = rangeSum + (high[jj] - low[jj]);
}
if ((int)lookback >= 1) {
    avgRange = rangeSum / (int)lookback;
}
climax = el_ge(high[0] - low[0], rangeMultiple * avgRange);
bigBody = el_gt(std::fabs(close[0] - open[0]), bodyMultiple * avgRange);
brokeUp = false;
brokeDn = false;
for (int kk = 1; kk <= (int)failBars; ++kk) {
    if ((int)lookback < 1) break;
    lvlLo = low[kk + 1];
    lvlHi = high[kk + 1];
    for (int jj = kk + 2; jj <= kk + (int)lookback; ++jj) {
        if (el_lt(low[jj], lvlLo)) lvlLo = low[jj];
        if (el_gt(high[jj], lvlHi)) lvlHi = high[jj];
    }
    if (el_lt(close[kk], lvlLo) && el_gt(close[0], lvlLo)) brokeDn = true;
    if (el_gt(close[kk], lvlHi) && el_lt(close[0], lvlHi)) brokeUp = true;
}
termUp = divUp || climax || (brokeUp && bigBody);
termDn = divDn || climax || (brokeDn && bigBody);
if (seenUp) ageUp = ageUp + 1;
if (termUp) {
    seenUp = true;
    ageUp = 0;
}
if (seenDn) ageDn = ageDn + 1;
if (termDn) {
    seenDn = true;
    ageDn = 0;
}
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
hiB1 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
hiB3 = -1.0;
loB1 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
loB3 = -1.0;
for (int pj = (int)strength; pj <= (int)pivotLookback - 1; ++pj) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int pk = pj - (int)strength; pk <= pj - 1; ++pk) {
        if (el_le(high[pj], high[pk])) okHi = false;
        if (el_ge(low[pj], low[pk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)strength; ++pk) {
        if (el_lt(high[pj], high[pk])) okHi = false;
        if (el_gt(low[pj], low[pk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) { hiPx1 = high[pj]; hiB1 = (double)pj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[pj]; hiB2 = (double)pj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[pj]; hiB3 = (double)pj; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) { loPx1 = low[pj]; loB1 = (double)pj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[pj]; loB2 = (double)pj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[pj]; loB3 = (double)pj; }
    }
}
legNew = hiPx1 - loPx1;
priorSum = hiPx2 - loPx2;
ordUp = el_lt(hiB1, loB1) && el_lt(loB1, hiB2) && el_lt(hiB2, loB2);
ordDn = el_lt(loB1, hiB1) && el_lt(hiB1, loB2) && el_lt(loB2, hiB2);
if (el_ge(numLegs, 2.0)) {
    priorSum = priorSum + (hiPx3 - loPx3);
    ordUp = ordUp && el_lt(loB2, hiB3) && el_lt(hiB3, loB3);
    ordDn = ordDn && el_lt(hiB2, loB3) && el_lt(loB3, hiB3);
}
haveLegs = el_ge(numLegs, 1.0) && el_ge((double)nHiPiv, numLegs + 1.0)
    && el_ge((double)nLoPiv, numLegs + 1.0) && el_gt(priorSum, 0.0);
legUpStrong = haveLegs && ordUp && el_ge(legNew * numLegs, legMultiple * priorSum);
legDnStrong = haveLegs && ordDn && el_ge(legNew * numLegs, legMultiple * priorSum);
haveSigUp = false;
haveSigDn = false;
sigHighUp = 0.0;
sigLowDn = 0.0;
for (int sj = 1; sj <= (int)maxWaitBars; ++sj) {
    // The twin guards this whole scan on `spikeBars >= 1` (EL's For would count
    // DOWN at 0), so the C++ must not run it either: with an empty inner loop
    // both spike flags would stay true and arm a signal EL never arms.
    if ((int)spikeBars < 1) break;
    bool spikeUpOk = true;
    bool spikeDnOk = true;
    for (int si = sj + 1; si <= sj + (int)spikeBars; ++si) {
        if (el_le(close[si], open[si])) spikeUpOk = false;
        if (el_lt(close[si] - open[si], bodyFraction * (high[si] - low[si]))) spikeUpOk = false;
        if (el_ge(close[si], open[si])) spikeDnOk = false;
        if (el_lt(open[si] - close[si], bodyFraction * (high[si] - low[si]))) spikeDnOk = false;
    }
    if (spikeUpOk && el_lt(low[sj], low[sj + 1])) {
        haveSigUp = true;
        sigHighUp = high[sj];
    }
    if (spikeDnOk && el_gt(high[sj], high[sj + 1])) {
        haveSigDn = true;
        sigLowDn = low[sj];
    }
}
trigUp = haveSigUp && el_gt(close[0], sigHighUp);
trigDn = haveSigDn && el_lt(close[0], sigLowDn);
